id: pm-4fwn0o
title: "MCP server cards and well-known metadata: discover identity, endpoints, capabilities, trust, and deployment facts before connecting"
description: Track the Server Card Working Group direction as a distinct interoperability capability. Publish bounded cacheable well-known metadata that lets hosts reason about a pm MCP server before transport negotiation while preventing information leakage and metadata drift.
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[6]: "area:mcp",discovery,interoperability,metadata,server-card,well-known
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:32.953Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:58:33.016Z"
deadline: "2027-06-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: A versioned server card declares identity endpoints supported protocol eras extensions authorization metadata and operational limits; fields are generated from the same SDK contracts as server discover and package manifests; signatures cache semantics rotation and stale metadata behavior are specified; unauthenticated metadata is minimized and cannot leak private workspace or capability state; HTTP and package-based discovery have conformance and downgrade tests; hosts can select or reject a server before opening a protocol request
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: high
confidence: low
